To render the Chulapa font with its ligatures in a heading, you must apply the font settings via custom CSS in `assets/css/custom.scss`. Ensure you preserve the empty YAML front matter at the top of the file.

```scss
---
---
h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
  font-feature-settings: "liga", "dlig";
  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
}
```

Note that the Chulapa font is bundled and does not require external loading. If you wish to apply the font and ligatures inline to specific text, you can use the `chulapa` class: `<span class="chulapa">Chulapa</span>`.

Sources:
* [Bundled font](https://dieghernan.github.io/chulapa/docs/53-chulapa-font)

After editing your configuration, restart Jekyll and perform a published-result check on your live site to verify the ligatures.
